  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Death comes with a bill, and it usually lands on the people you leave behind. Let's rank what it actually costs.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "building",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "What dying",
            "costs."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "An average US death now runs over ten thousand dollars, all in.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "building",
          "big": "$10,000+",
          "label": "average US death, all in",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A traditional funeral is one of the largest single costs.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-funeral",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · funeral"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The choice of burial versus cremation alone swings it enormously.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "building",
          "big": "$2K vs $12K",
          "label": "cremation vs traditional burial",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A direct cremation can cost a fraction of a full burial.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-cremation",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · cremation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Then comes probate, the legal process of settling the estate, which can eat three to seven percent of it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "vault",
          "big": "3–7%",
          "label": "of the estate, to probate",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Probate is the court process that validates a will and pays debts.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-probate",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · probate"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A little planning, a will and the right accounts, can save your family most of that cost and chaos.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Planning saves it",
          "props": [
            "check",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Grief is hard enough without a surprise five-figure bill arriving right on top of it.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Grief + a bill",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And a large estate can face taxes before heirs see a cent.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-estatetax",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · estate tax"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s10"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So, have you actually planned for any of that?",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "question",
          "art": "building",
          "line": "Have you planned?",
          "sub": "Comment honestly"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s11"
    }
  ]
